# Check out every text file with LF line endings, on every platform.
#
# Everything in this repository runs on Linux or inside Linux containers:
# shell and Python scripts, the devcontainer Dockerfile and the files it COPYs
# (scanner pins, rule sources, dnsmasq allowlists), and the fake binaries the
# FSM tests put on PATH. On a Windows host with core.autocrlf=true, a CRLF
# checkout makes the kernel read "bash\r" from the shebang, so an image build
# fails with exit 127 (seen at fetch-semgrep-rules.sh) and pinned values gain a
# trailing \r.
#
# cfgms's own .gitattributes cannot cover this: Git does not apply a parent
# repository's attributes inside a submodule.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files are never rewritten.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary
*.exe  binary
